.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH mnnn-journal 1  "mnnn-journal 2.11.1" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-journal \- Journals: entries in Markdown or LaTeX with images, notes and highlights
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn journal\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Journals: entries in Markdown or LaTeX with images, notes and highlights
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-list(1)
List journals (standalone and in projects)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-new(1)
Create a journal, standalone or in a project
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-show(1)
Show a journal: notes, entries, highlights and images (\-\-json: the whole document)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-edit(1)
Rename a journal or change the format for new entries
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-remove(1)
Remove a journal with its entries, notes, highlights and images
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-fork(1)
Fork a journal (everything in it) into a project\-specific journal
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-write(1)
Write a new entry
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-entry(1)
Show one entry with its notes, highlights and images
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-edit\-entry(1)
Change an entry\*(Aqs title, text or format (notes and highlights follow their words)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-remove\-entry(1)
Remove an entry
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-copy(1)
Add selected entries (copies) to another journal or a new one
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-note(1)
Add a note to a journal, an entry, or selected words of an entry
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-highlight(1)
Highlight selected words of an entry
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-edit\-note(1)
Change a note\*(Aqs text (or a highlight\*(Aqs comment)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-remove\-note(1)
Remove a note or highlight
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-attach(1)
Attach an image to an entry (stored in the database; a reference is added to the text)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-image(1)
Write an attached image to a file
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-export(1)
Export a journal (or some entries) as PDF, Word, HTML, LaTeX, text or JSON (JSON can be imported again)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-import(1)
Import a journal exported as JSON (as a new journal)
.TP
mnnn\-journal\-print(1)
Print a journal (or some entries): a PDF sent to lp/lpr, or saved if there is none
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.11.1
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
